# A suite in the format verdict reads. One JSON object per line; blank lines
# and lines starting with # are skipped. Only "prompt" is required.
#
#   case_id     stable, and the seed for everything reproducible about the
#               case -- change it and you have a different case
#   prompt      what the pipeline is asked
#   reference   optional; shown to the judge, which may be empty
#   tags        the slices the gate reports separately. Four metrics across
#               four tags is sixteen comparisons, which is where the
#               multiplicity problem comes from -- a tag with fewer than
#               min_slice cases is not tested on its own.
#   difficulty  synthetic suites only, and ignored for real ones. It is the
#               latent difficulty the simulated pipelines read.
#
# Any other key is kept in the case's meta, so a ticket id or an owner can
# ride along without this file needing to know about it.
